<title>USA: Old America Stores CEO resigns.</title>
<headline>Old America Stores CEO resigns.</headline>
<dateline>HOWE, Texas 1997-06-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Old America Stores Inc said Friday its board has accepted the resignation of chief executive officer Richard Tredinnick.</p>
<p>The company said it has named chief operating officer Jerry Payton as interim chief executive.</p>
<p>The announcement came as the company reported a first quarter loss of $2.99 million or $0.66 per share and as the company unveiled an austerity program that includes the closing of up to 25 of its 102 retail stores.</p>
